From 4c0dd29eb15b2cef5cf5256459a19d59e5c98adc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Ye <allen.ye@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 22 Dec 2023 18:09:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 120/126] mtk: hostapd: Add txpower vendor command

Add the lpi_psd and lpi_bcn_enhance configuration items and send them
to the driver with the MediaTek txpower vendor command when the
interface setup completes. lpi_psd turns on the 6 GHz LPI PSD power
compensation. lpi_bcn_enhance makes the driver send 6 GHz management
frames as 80 MHz non-HT duplicates. The command carries the wiphy
radio index of the hardware that the interface uses, because mt7996
rejects it without one. hostapd leaves the index out before it
selects that hardware, and when the wiphy reports no radios. There is
no SKU index item, because no mt76 driver reads the SKU index
attribute.

mt76 sends the duplicate only on an operating channel of 80 MHz or
wider, so the Duplicate Beacon bit of the 6 GHz Operation Information
is set only there, as IEEE Std 802.11-2024 requires. The driver
writes the beacon TX descriptor when a beacon is set and keeps the
old setting across a restart, so hostapd sets 6 GHz beacons again
after the command. A command that the driver refuses is logged, and
the AP stays up.

Signed-off-by: Allen Ye <allen.ye@mediatek.com>
Co-developed-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
